        "prohibited_concomitant": [
          "Anticholinergic agents (any route - IV, oral, inhaled, topical, including topical glycopyrrolate or derivatives) used to treat hyperhidrosis, asthma, incontinence, gastrointestinal cramps, or muscular spasms are prohibited throughout the study.",
          "Any oral or topical homeopathic or herbal treatment (e.g., sage tablets, chamomile, valerian root, St. John's wort) is prohibited.",
          "Any prescription topical product, including prescription topical antiperspirants or similar agents (e.g., Drysol, Xerac AC, Certain DRI), and hand sanitizers applied to the axillae are prohibited for the duration of the study.",
          "Any other treatment or procedure for axillary hyperhidrosis is prohibited, including botulinum toxin, thermolysis (e.g., MiraDry, laser, or other), sympathectomy, or iontophoresis.",
          "Any surgical procedure involving the axillae (including laser hair removal), or any surgical procedure resulting in significant axillary scarring, is prohibited.",
          "Oral cholinergic agents (e.g., bethanechol) are prohibited throughout the study.",
          "Addition of, or dose change for, serotonergic agonists/SSRIs, beta-blockers, alpha-adrenergic agonists (clonidine), dopamine partial agonists, tricyclic antidepressants, anti-anxiety/antidepressant drugs, amphetamine products, or other drugs with known anticholinergic side effects is prohibited during the study.",
          "Over-the-counter topical antiperspirant/deodorant applied directly to the axilla(e) is prohibited within 7 days of GSP1 (Visit 2) and for the duration of the study; Sponsor-supplied non-antiperspirant deodorant is provided instead."
        ],
        "permitted_concomitant": [
          "Therapy considered necessary for the subject's welfare may be given at the Investigator's discretion (Section 6.1); if the permissibility of a specific medication/treatment is in question, the Medical Monitor is contacted.",
          "A subject on a stable dose (per Investigator judgment) of a serotonergic agonist/SSRI, beta-blocker, alpha-adrenergic agonist, dopamine partial agonist, or tricyclic antidepressant for >=3 months with no recent change in hyperhidrosis frequency/severity may continue that medication at an unaltered dose during the study.",
          "A subject on a stable dose of an anti-anxiety and/or anti-depressant drug for >=3 months with no recent change in hyperhidrosis frequency/severity may continue that medication; psychostimulants may likewise be allowed if the dose has been stable for >=3 months without a change in hyperhidrosis frequency/severity.",
          "Drugs with known anticholinergic side effects (e.g., dry mouth, blurred vision) taken within the last 28 days may be allowed at the Investigator's discretion, provided the dose is not altered during the study.",
          "Sponsor-supplied non-antiperspirant deodorant may be applied, but not within 8 hours following study product application.",
          "Prior axillary laser hair removal is permitted if performed more than 28 days before GSP1 (Visit 2)."
        ],
