        "study_drug_doses_mg": [],
        "population_note": "A multicenter, randomized, double-blind, vehicle-controlled Phase 3 trial (\"Cardigan II\") of sofpironium bromide gel, 15% applied topically once daily at bedtime to both axillae for 42 consecutive days in subjects >=9 years old with primary axillary hyperhidrosis -- the twin trial to Cardigan I (BBI-4000-CL-301/NCT03836287), sharing an identical protocol design and concomitant-medication rules. This is a simple monotherapy-vs-vehicle design with no standardized background regimen; the real content is a set of prohibited/permitted concomitant medication and treatment rules (Protocol Sections 6.1-6.2) rather than an AD/psoriasis-style background topical regimen."
