        "rationale": "No rescue-medication/rescue-therapy concept exists in this monotherapy-vs-vehicle design. Protocol Section 6.2 (Prohibited Medications/Treatments) affirmatively prohibits any treatment or procedure for axillary hyperhidrosis throughout the study -- including botulinum toxin, thermolysis (e.g., MiraDry, laser), sympathectomy, iontophoresis -- as well as any prescription topical antiperspirant/similar agent (e.g., Drysol, Xerac AC, Certain DRI) and any over-the-counter topical antiperspirant/deodorant applied to the axillae (Sponsor-supplied non-antiperspirant deodorant is provided instead). A subject with inadequate response has no protocol-sanctioned escalation option within the study; the SAP and protocol contain no 'rescue' or 'escape' provision anywhere in the document (confirmed via full-text keyword search). Identical design/rule set to the twin trial Cardigan I (NCT03836287)."
